WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.360
More than 30% of UK diesel imports are American, and a ban could lift prices there. This is Omni View, episode

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:14.420
193. President Donald Trump has said he may ask European countries to release diesel held in reserve,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:21.800
and he is considering a ban on American exports of that fuel, the BBC reports. A ban is a government stop

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:28.780
on shipping the fuel out. A reserve release is stored fuel put back on sale. Neither step has been taken

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:35.240
yet. He is asking, and he is weighing the restriction. Prices had already jumped after the war in Iran

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:42.020
disrupted supplies. Diesel is the fuel farms, truck fleets, and a wide run of other businesses burn,

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:48.300
so a spike shows up in the cost of work that cannot wait. Scott Besent, the Treasury Secretary,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:54.160
the Cabinet Officer who speaks for United States Economic Policy, urged Europe to make additional

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:59.760
supplies available immediately. His case is that American farmers, truckers, and businesses

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:05.160
should not bear the full burden of a shortage made somewhere else. If exports stop,

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:11.280
barrels that now leave American ports stay in the home market. The reporting says that extra supply

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.560
could bring prices down for American drivers. Specialists in the same account warn of the

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.680
mirror image abroad. Importing countries would face added pressure on prices unless other supplies are

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:28.180
found to replace the American barrels. Martin McCluskey, the United Kingdom's energy minister,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.080
has held calls with European partners to prepare a coordinated response. He has noted reserves

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:39.680
still on hand from an earlier release. That is the response already in motion. Phone calls

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:45.460
among European capitals and stocks that were drawn once before. The British government states there

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:51.380
is no cause for concern about shortages. It still expects prices to rise further. The threat,

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:55.400
Met the request and the price split all sit ahead of elections in November.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.720
Thousands of people gathered in Central Delhi to demand that Chief Election Commissioner

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.200
Ganesh Kumar resign over names deleted from the voter lists, Deutscheweller reports,

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.680
and it casts the protest as renewed pressure on Prime Minister Narendra Modi's government.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:17.580
Police had refused permission for the gathering at Jantar Montar, a long-used protest ground

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.860
in the capital, and then tighten security around the site.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:26.220
The Chief Election Commissioner leads the commission that runs India's elections, a body

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.380
meant to stand independent of whichever party is in power.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.500
Electoral roles are the official lists of people allowed to vote.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.100
Names were removed.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.100
That part is not in dispute.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:42.160
Wearing accounts split is what those removals were for, and how they were chosen.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.480
The BJP has dismissed the protesters' claims.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:51.060
names. Its case is that cleaning the lists protects the election itself. Dead voters and

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:56.440
people it calls illegal infiltrators should not remain on a wall, because ineligible names

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.880
are how fraud gets a ballot. Opposition leaders argue the deletions

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.460
fall disproportionately on minority voters. Their case is that the commission has not published

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:12.480
clear criteria for removal or the outcomes of appeals, so a legitimate voter has no plain

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.880
way to see a fair cleanup rather than a lost vote. Critics add a 2023 law that gave the

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.620
government a greater say in appointing the Chief Commissioner, which makes independence harder

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:29.360
to take on trust. Inside the commission, two of the three election commissioners raised formal

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:36.020
concerns about the revision process at least 14 times. That record sits in the files of the institution

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:42.180
the government says is simply administering the lists. Police in London have arrested a 25-year-old

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:47.740
man who was a citizen of both the United Kingdom and Iran, on suspicion of preparing terrorist

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:54.320
acts, the Hindu reports. The arrest followed a major incident at RAF Fairford, a royal

00:03:54.320 --> 00:04:00.100
Air Force base that US forces had used for operations related to Iran. Five other men,

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:05.400
arrested earlier, have been released on bail, which means they are free while the inquiry continues.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.520
No explosives were found at the scene. Officials have not explained what the threat actually was.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.960
The dispute over responsibility runs through that gap.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:20.000
Prime Minister Andy Burnham said there were strong indications that Iran played a part

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.220
in the weekend incident.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:26.760
His statement treats the indications as serious enough to say in public, while the physical

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.400
picture officials will describe is still incomplete.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.200
Iran called the accusations baseless.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.680
It condemned Britain for allowing its bases to be used in U.S.-Israeli actions, which

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.980
is Iran's account of who widened the conflict onto British soil.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.760
Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu told Fox News that Israel had given Britain

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.420
intelligence about an Iranian-sponsored plot.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:55.460
Three capitals are assigning a role or denying one, while the arrest stands and the nature

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.200
of the threat remains unexplained.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.140
Several arrests have been made in a Turkish stock market case that touched nearly half a

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:04.460
million investors, Don Chavella reports.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.600
Stock work at manipulation means trading built to push prices away from what ordinary

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.100
binary buying and selling would have set. Nearly half a million people is a crowd the

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:19.280
size of a large city, each of them with money in the market the case disturbed. A woman

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.400
politician from the ruling AKP, Turkey's governing party, resigned in connection with

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.120
the case. The scandal has prompted questions about oversight of the country's financial

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:33.800
markets, meaning the rules and the watchdogs that are supposed to catch this kind of trading

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:39.040
before it spreads. The government has not detailed how large the losses were. It has

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:44.640
not detailed the exact methods used, what it has done is make arrests and accept a resignation

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:49.380
from inside the governing party. Those steps are the official effort to answer investor

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:54.800
concern while the investigation continues. China aims to expand its intelligent computing

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:00.320
capacity more than fourfold from the level at the end of June to hit a goal set for 2030,

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:06.660
the South China Morning Post reports. Intelligent computing capacity is the raw computing power used

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.380
to train and run artificial intelligence or AI.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.920
Fourfold means more than four times the June level,

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.620
not a small add-on to what is already installed.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.080
The target arrives while the country faces United States

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.260
restrictions on advanced AI chips,

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.800
the hardware that does much of that computing.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:28.220
Capacity grew 177% in the year to June,

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.220
which is the recent pace the plan is trying to extend.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.440
The paper says meeting the goal will take innovation,

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.920
adaptation, and the coordination of vast resources.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:44.080
It frames the target as a test of whether development at home can offset limits on what can be imported.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:51.260
Novartis will license a messenger RNA therapy for autoimmune disease from China's Abagen Biosciences,

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.900
in a deal worth up to $7.8 billion Bloomberg reports.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:00.320
A license means Novartis pays for the right to take the therapy forward,

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.840
rather than buying the Chinese firm outright.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:02.940
Right.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:09.160
Messenger RNA, often shortened to messenger RNA, is a set of instructions a cell can read.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:14.900
The same approach, already proven in vaccines, is now being aimed at autoimmune conditions,

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:18.760
illnesses in which the body's own defenses turn on its tissues.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:25.680
Up to $7.8 billion is the ceiling of the agreement, not a sum that necessarily changes hands

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:26.380
on day one.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:32.020
Bloomberg calls it one of the largest cross-border biotech licensing deals involving a Chinese

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:36.760
company. The paper reads the agreement as evidence that Chinese firms are building

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:42.220
real capability in advanced therapeutics, the medicines at the complicated end of the industry.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:47.440
Seven hours and 55 minutes from launch to a docking is progress worth knowing,

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:52.020
and it is the fastest American flight to the International Space Station on record.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:57.780
Dewey Tevella reports that the Crew 13 team finished the journey faster than earlier missions.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:02.620
stations. The station is the shared laboratory in orbit where crews live and work for months

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:08.520
at a time. Docking is the moment the arriving craft locks on. The shorter trip reflects

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:13.860
ongoing improvements in launch and rendezvous procedures. The timing of lift-off and the

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:19.480
path flown to meet the station. Less time in transit means crews spend fewer hours getting

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:25.300
there. It also frees more resources for operations once they are aboard, so more of the mission

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.060
is the work of the station rather than the ride up.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:33.940
To really understand an export ban, follow the cargo rather than the announcement because

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:38.620
diesel trades on a global spot market, where a ship can be sent somewhere new in a day.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.420
Price is the signal.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:43.140
A cargo does not stay loyal to one buyer.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:47.840
It goes to whoever bids more, and that choice is remade as prices move.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:52.820
When a major exporter holds barrels back, importers have two practical moves.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:58.020
They can bid higher in some other port, or they can draw down reserves of their own.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:03.220
Those reserves are sized for a short break in supply, not for a shortfall that lasts.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:07.520
The United States holds strategic reserves under government control.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:13.240
It also has commercial stocks, and refiners release those according to profit margins, not

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.800
because a minister tells them to.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.580
A ban can change what leaves the country.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:22.820
It does not, by itself, order private stocks onto the market at a political price.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.580
European countries keep government-controlled stocks under rules from the international

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.260
energy agency, or IEA.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:33.500
Those rules call for 90 days of net imports.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.620
Releasing the stocks takes a coordinated political decision, and that decision can lag a price spike

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.720
by enough time for drivers and firms to feel the jump first.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:46.460
Volume is how you tell a gesture from a change in the market.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:54.000
it. American diesel exports run between 1.2 and 1.5 million barrels a day. Set any announced

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.200
ban or release beside the daily export figures from the U.S. Energy Information Administration,

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:05.300
the agency that publishes those flows. If the announced barrels are small next to that daily

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:16.440
trade, the price move is coming from somewhere else. Primary figures from that agency and from

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.960
from an exporting country and an importing country

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.060
will often describe one set of barrels

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:22.820
in two very different tones.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.840
Reading the BBC next to Bloomberg on today's diesel story

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.500
is the way to see those two frames on the same events.

